# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current phase doc before changing code.

Work only on the current phase. The current phase is Phase 10. See [docs/phase-10.md](docs/phase-10.md).

Do feature work on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Phase 10 may add a jurisdiction transfer adapter, Queensland profile fields, generated and stored application PDFs, admin review of an offline signed pack, and manual Fisheries Queensland tracking. Do not add live e-sign, an FQ API, live Stripe keys, seller bank payouts, refund/chargeback workflows, or other jurisdictions’ real processes. Never trust the browser for payment status, bid time, quota availability, or transfer outcome. Never delete quota ledger rows.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture.

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current phase.

Stop at the end of each phase. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
